:Does anyone know if there is an intrinsic ability conferring paralysis
:resistance, and how said intrinsic is acquired?  I had a pretty good game
:going, dlevel 26, Medusa dead, lots of goodies.  Next this gelatinous cube
:paralyzes me and a yellow dragon proceeds to nuke my cookies.  And I had a pet
:djinn with 300-odd hit points, too!  Rats!
     A hint: gelatinous cubes can't paralyze you unless you attack
them, and they don't do much damage.  So don't attack them unless you
can somehow ensure that you won't be attacked in a short amount of time.
Being invisible and checking (via blindfold) for nearby monsters is 
a good way of going about it.  Backing yourself into the end of a
corridor will also do it, although make sure there aren't any dwarves
(this won't work for a floating eye, btw-- they paralyze you for just
too damn long, so there's still a good change that a dwarf will appear
and tunnel towards you).  Earth elementals and Xorns can also get you,
although if you're invisible none of them are likely to.
     The *safest* way is to kill it with missile weapons, of course.
     I personally find that missile weapons are a lot easier to use
given invisibility myself, although monsters are still able to throw
them back straight at you.  Another thing I don't like is that monsters
can do three things in one round: move, pick something up, and throw it
at you.  While you can move and pick up in one round, I think it unfair
that monsters can move and fire in one; it totally screws up the game
balance as far as missile fire.  Nymphs can zig-zag towards you and
avoid being hit (even if you're polymorphed into a dragon), while
zigzagging towards a dragon will get you fried nevertheless.

